  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: all 8 refill messages are closed and every patient who wrote got a reply.\n\n- Samuel Price (pt-0030)\n  - Metformin 1000 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0002). His kidney function (eGFR) is 58, and his HbA1c was 7.1% at an outside lab on 2026-08-19. The patient asked once and the pharmacy asked twice. I treated these as one request and placed one order.\n  - Lisinopril 20 mg: I first renewed it for 90 days (mr-t0001). At 08:00 the lab corrected his 10/06 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49. That is 35% above his 1.10 before the 09/18 dose increase, which the protocol treats like a potassium of 5.5 or higher. I cancelled mr-t0001 and created an urgent task for you (focus mr-00295). He has no active lisinopril order, and I sent him a corrected message.\n- Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg\n  - His 08/27 outside potassium of 5.9 was on a hemolyzed (damaged) sample, so it didn't count. On his 01/20 potassium of 4.5 I renewed for 90 days (mr-t0003) and ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0004).\n  - A new St. Brigid report then arrived: potassium 5.8 on an acceptable sample collected 10/20. I cancelled mr-t0003 and created an urgent task for you (focus mr-00283). He has no active lisinopril order, and I sent him a corrected message.\n  - The repeat BMP order is still open. Please decide whether he still needs it.\n- Marcus Webb (pt-0031)\n  - Lisinopril 10 mg: 30-day supply with no refills (mr-t0005), and I ordered a BMP (sr-t0006). His last BMP was collected 2025-10-20, so none falls within 12 months; his last visit was 2026-09-28.\n  - Metformin 500 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). His eGFR is 92 and his HbA1c is 6.9%. A 10/14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error (mislabelled specimen), so I didn't use it.\n  - A potassium of 4.6 drawn on its own arrived during the work. It isn't a BMP, so the decision stands.\n- Leonard Kaplan (pt-0070), lisinopril 20 mg: not refilled. His 10/19 creatinine of 1.46 is 46% above his 1.00 before the 09/28 dose increase. I created an urgent task for you (focus mr-70002) and told him you will review it.\n\nI wrote chart notes documenting the reversals for Price and Odum. Three items that arrived this morning (the Price creatinine correction, the Odum outside report and the Webb potassium) are still open in your results queue. I acted on them here but did not close them. I did not touch the other open items in your results queue (other patients) because they were outside this request; some are flagged critical, including potassiums of 6.3 (pt-0016) and 6.4 (pt-0008), and still need your review.",
